menu "Sprout feature modules"

config FEATURE_FACTORY_RESET
    bool "Enable guarded local factory reset"
    default y
    depends on FEATURE_MODULE_REGISTRY
    help
        Require an explicit second confirmation before erasing the device's own
        configuration and credentials. A pending request expires after a
        bounded timeout. The reset never erases application or data partitions
        other than the configured NVS partition.

config FACTORY_RESET_PENDING_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
    int "Pending request timeout in seconds"
    depends on FEATURE_FACTORY_RESET
    range 1 300
    default 10
    help
        A bare request is rejected once this many seconds pass without an
        explicit confirmation, so an accidental gesture cannot leave the
        device armed indefinitely.

config FACTORY_RESET_LOCAL_CONFIRM_WINDOW_SECONDS
    int "Local confirmation window in seconds"
    depends on FEATURE_FACTORY_RESET
    range 1 120
    default 5
    help
        After a local request, the secondary button must be short-pressed
        within this window to confirm the erase. The primary button cancels
        while the request is armed. This is separate from the overall pending
        request timeout so an accidental gesture cannot erase by itself.

config FACTORY_RESET_NVS_PARTITION
    string "NVS partition erased by factory reset"
    depends on FEATURE_FACTORY_RESET
    default "nvs"
    help
        Label of the device-owned NVS partition. Only this partition is
        erased. Keep it identical to the partition used by config_store and
        device identity so credentials do not remain on the device.

endmenu
